This repository holds the code and per-case results of the paper "Find the Missing Skill, Build the Data: Targeted
Data Sets for pi0.5 on LIBERO-Plus". Its code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Third-party works that this code uses, none of which is redistributed here:

- LIBERO-Plus (benchmark, simulator fork at commit 4976dc30, assets): camera-render/cameras/transform.py reimplements
  the camera transform of the fork's problem classes from their documented behaviour and copies no code from it; the
  fork has no licence file. The base camera poses in that file are numeric values read from the fork. The case names,
  factors and levels in results/ identify the benchmark's test cases. To run the render code you need your own copy
  of the fork and its assets, from their source.
- LIBERO (demonstrations: Apache-2.0 on their card; code: MIT).
- openpi (Physical Intelligence, Apache-2.0) and RLinf (Apache-2.0): the encoder-stage hooks in encoder-stage/hooks/ plug into a
  trainer built on them; neither is included.
- FLUX-3 Action (Black Forest Labs, black-forest-labs/flux-3-action-base at revision 62878e29, FLUX Kommunity
  License v1.0): results/flux3-plus-only and results/flux3-mix hold the per-case success flags of two fine-tunes of
  it, which we fine-tuned and evaluated for non-commercial research only. No FLUX-3 weights, fine-tunes or other
  outputs are in this repository. Black Forest Labs does not endorse this work.

Model outputs in this repository, released with the results under Apache-2.0:

- language/rewriter/table-gpt.json holds outputs of OpenAI's GPT-6-astra, and table-qwen.json outputs of Qwen3.5-9B
  (Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B at revision c2022362, Apache-2.0 on its model card). Neither model is included. Each table
  rewrites the LIBERO-Plus instruction of every test case. The rewrites of the 1,537 language cases are derived from
  the benchmark's language test instructions, for which we found no licence; those instructions themselves are not
  in this repository, as for language/decoded-prompts.jsonl. On the other 8,493 cases, 8,473 GPT rewrites and 7,978
  Qwen rewrites equal the case's LIBERO task instruction (LIBERO: MIT code, Apache-2.0 demonstrations).

The model weights are not in this repository. Those of mxri-va (the main weights) and of mxri-lg-va-1 are a Model
Derivative of Gemma and are released separately, at huggingface.co/alakazamworld/pi05-libero-plus-targeted. Gemma is provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms of Use found at ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
